      "remarks": "Secure Endpoint is a composite pattern expressing the institutional position that endpoints are acceptable execution environments for institutional use. This assertion is valid only when endpoints are recognized and managed, securely configured, continuously evaluated for health and compliance, protected at runtime from threats, and deliberately managed through their lifecycle.\n\nGovernance and Responsibility Anchor:\nThis pattern serves as the enterprise endpoint trust statement. It introduces no independent controls. A system may assert use of a secure endpoint only if all referenced constituent endpoint patterns are realized and assessed."
    },

